text:
lucy: Hey all, trying to use the JS SDK in an Expo + Hermes app and hitting two issues: Metro resolves the ESM entry (exports.import -> dist/index.mjs) which pulls in node-only crypto and stream code, and TypeScript drags node lib types because the SDK d.ts references node:stream. Anyone have a minimal set of fixes that doesn't require forking the SDK?

diego: Metro will follow the exports/import field by default. If the package has a `react-native` or `main` pointing to CJS, Metro picks that instead. Short term you can alias the module to the CJS file.

nina: Alias example we use:```js
// metro.config.js
const path = require('path')
module.exports = {
  resolver: {
    extraNodeModules: {
      'my-sdk$': path.resolve(__dirname, 'node_modules/my-sdk/dist/index.cjs')
    }
  }
}
```

lucy: Thanks — that fixed the Metro bundling. Runtime still fails because global.crypto.getRandomValues and ReadableStream are undefined. Hermes complains on Symbol.asyncIterator too.

tara: For crypto we landed on `react-native-get-random-values` + `expo-random` fallback. For streams, `web-streams-polyfill/ponyfill` works but you need to wire Symbol.asyncIterator for Hermes sometimes. Minimal shims at app entry:```js
import 'react-native-get-random-values';
import 'abortcontroller-polyfill/dist/abortcontroller-polyfill-only';
const {ReadableStream} = require('web-streams-polyfill/ponyfill');
if (!global.ReadableStream) global.ReadableStream = ReadableStream;
if (!Symbol.asyncIterator) Symbol.asyncIterator = Symbol.for('asyncIterator');
```

diego: Oof on the Symbol hack — it's yucky but pragmatic until SDK publishes a RN build. Also watch for code paths that use `for await (const chunk of stream)`; if the polyfill doesn't provide async iterator you need to adapt those call sites.

nina: TS pain: we set `skipLibCheck: true` to unblock, but I filed a small local d.ts shim in the app to avoid pulling Node types:```ts
declare module 'node:stream' {
  export type Readable = any;
}

lucy: What should we ask the SDK team for in an issue/PR? I can open one with the repro.

tara: Request list: 1) add a `react-native` package.json entry that points to a RN-friendly build (CJS or UMD) 2) ensure `exports` has a `require` fallback for packagers that prefer CJS 3) publish a browser/edge build without Node native deps and a small RN build with docs 4) provide separate type defs that avoid `node:` imports or conditional types 5) mention RN/Expo in README and common metro/workarounds

diego: +1. Also ask for small runtime feature flags so consumers can disable streaming or Node-only adapters at build time (tree-shakeable). That makes a tiny RN bundle possible.

expo-bot: Note: Expo SDK 48+ surfaces `crypto.getRandomValues` in managed runtime. Custom dev clients and older SDKs may still need polyfills. See https://blog.expo.dev/ for details.

nina: I'll add a repro gist: expo init blank -> enable Hermes -> yarn add my-sdk react-native-get-random-values web-streams-polyfill abortcontroller-polyfill -> add shims at App entry -> run on Android emulator. Include metro logs showing it picked the mjs file, tsconfig error output, and a short app that reproduces the runtime crash.

lucy: Perfect — I'll open the issue and link the repro + proposed PR that adds a `react-native` build and lighter browser bundle. If anyone has tiny diff suggestions for the PR I can include them.
tara: I can add the metro snippet and the minimal shims to the issue so maintainers can copy-paste. Also include a note about Symbol.asyncIterator on Hermes.
diego: One more tip: if you can't alias in Metro, you can import the CJS build explicitly in RN code: `const SDK = require('my-sdk/dist/index.cjs')` — works for quick hacks.

lucy: Thanks everyone — saved my afternoon. Will paste the issue link when it's up :thumbsup:
